    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Gunnar Henderson** stands as our premier play with an elite score of 81.88. His massive projection is bolstered by a favorable 4.41 xERA matchup against L\u00f3pez and a 14% boost from his dynamic platoon advantage, making him the anchor of the Austin Waves lineup. Both **Drake Baldwin** (71.83) and **Jackson Merrill** (71.56) follow closely as strong starts; **Drake Baldwin** benefits from a high-efficiency batting order spot leading off and a 16% park factor uplift, while **Jackson Merrill** leverages a 14% SP skill advantage and a strong platoon split to capitalize on Junk\u2019s vulnerability. **Kyle Tucker** remains a reliable start at 64.35, despite a slight park penalty, as his inherent base value keeps his ceiling high even in a neutral matchup against Peralta.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, whose 47.58 score narrowly missed the cutoff. While **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** offered respectable potential, he was squeezed out by the sheer volume of high-efficiency alternatives in our infield and utility spots; specifically, the negative impact of his dynamic platoon against Drake and a low batting order priority tipped the scales in favor of the higher-ceiling options like **Jacob Wilson** (62.27). Managers should monitor the weather closely, specifically the wind factors; while **Denzer Guzman** (53.32) and **Heliot Ramos** (55.10) receive modest boosts from winds blowing out, any shift in these conditions could dampen their effectiveness. Conversely, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (63.39) is dealing with an \"In\" wind penalty, though his robust base projection keeps him in the starting nine regardless of the external conditions.",
